Sharding

horizontal scaling
supports distributed ACID transactions

increases volume of persisted data

increase/distribute throughput to scale both reads and writes

decrease latency of reads and writes

when should you shard?
above 200GB to 0.5TB and growing
hardware at its max limit
vertical scaling not possible or cost effective
your schema and cost maybe already have been optimized

when not to
below 200GB and not growing

Shard Key
used to route operations to the appropriate shard
used for reads and writes

Shard distribution is ideally even. but each has their own tradeoffs

Chunking
contiguous range of shard key values

Cardinality
number of unique fields. High cardinality lead to better distribution of documents in shards

Right distribution of shard key for documents load
Right distribution of writes
Right distribution of reads

Example a social media influencer has different content across their account. posts, media, content
One single shard key for the user may still be too concentrated
by using a compound shard key for different dates, could better distribute the load

Index locality
how indexes for large data sets are loaded into RAM has an impact
using both user and timestamp like in the social influencer example would better distribute the data as well for index locality

